{"Title":"An Act relative to reimbursement to armed service members","BillNumber":"S2331","DocketNumber":"SD1024","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T11:01:23.777"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T11:01:23.7766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2331/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Lewis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2331) of Jason M. Lewis for legislation relative to reimbursement to armed service members.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSection 59 of chapter 33 of the General Laws is hereby amended by striking subsection (e) and inserting in place thereof the following:-\r\n\t(e) An employee of a county, city or town which shall be entitled to the benefits and protections of this section or the benefits of the accepted earlier law.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}